    "created_at": "2020-09-09T07:50:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-09T07:50:49Z",
    "body": "The data model already guarantees it, no? It ends up ending with %00, not U+0000. Which is also why it seems reasonable to allow the parser to do that transformation for you if you want it.\r\n\r\nI doubt we can change the API generally and given that the API is for individual components it's already a very different proposition. Why should `port` trim them, for instance?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
